 4. Spirit&#x27;s data afterlife 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Maura Kearns/Axios.

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Google is acquiring Spirit Airlines' emails, calendar info, chats, documents, spreadsheets and other business data, according to a bankruptcy court filing .

 It will use the data to improve its products and AI models. Why it matters: Spirit Airlines ceased operations earlier this year after it failed to emerge from its second Chapter 11 bankruptcy , but attorneys are still handling the disposition of its assets.

 Zoom in: Google won a bankruptcy auction for the data, agreeing to pay $10 million for the information.

 The data does not contain any personally identifiable information, according to a court filing by PJT Partners vice president Dylan Friesner, an investment banker for Spirit. By the numbers: The deal includes about 100 million emails and 500 million Microsoft Teams chats, according to a court filing .

 It does not include passenger profiles or their frequent flyer information. State of play: Google is expected to use the data as fodder for large language model training.

